<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="c191c953">&lt;p&gt;
    Even with a detailed Benefits Realization Plan, there is still no guarantee that benefits will be realized. To increase
    the likelihood of benefits being realized as intended, it is crucial that there is effective execution of the benefits
    realization plan. This requires a number of elements to be in place:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Tracking of the key enabler milestones in the program plan
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Workstream leads understanding impact of their delivery on benefits
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Effective use of program risk/issue log to show impacts on benefits
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Regular time with Program Sponsors/Managers to discuss benefits realization progress, risks and issues.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The key questions that should be asked while developing a Benefits Realization Plan are as following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../practice.pm.delv.benefit_realiz_track.base/tasks/resources/Benefits Realization Plan - Key Questions.png&quot; width=&quot;600&quot; height=&quot;464&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="dffbd976"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="528891d"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="4ef9a856">&lt;p&gt;
    Show how benefits will be realized by developing a plan, which includes key tasks, milestones, roles and
    responsibilities for realizing the program benefits and&amp;nbsp;the timeline for when benefits will be realized. Package
    elements of the Benefits Realization Plan so that individuals and workstreams can understand their contribution. Ensure
    that each of the individuals outlined in the Benefits Realization Plan understands the role that he or she has in
    contributing to the specific benefit being realized.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The business case is analyzed to determine how benefits and cost savings will be realized over transformation time
    horizon and by key milestones. To build this plan additional task dependency analysis is conducted. Overall benefits
    realization plan should not differ significantly between programs, however it ensures that all significant milestones
    and tasks are identified. The plan links the identified benefits with drivers and business case, determine how the
    right data will be collected and when to measure and report results. The latest program benefit dependency map could
    also be used as an input into this plan as&amp;nbsp;the plan&amp;nbsp;should show both technical and business change enablers.
    Ownership and timing for each of these items should be captured in the plan. It should also incorporate key milestones
    and tasks from the program deployment and change management plans so that it summarizes the key enablers that
    contribute to program benefit realization.&amp;nbsp;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
